Z||000052||Black88GT||12-16-2000||06:29 PM||||Cutter, the MR2 turbo puts out 200 Hp and 200 lb. ft. of torque, with a TURBO.  A 3.4 puts out approx. 175 (newer G/A's) and 230 lb. ft. of torque NATURALLY ASPIRATED.  Your too dumb to realize there is a difference.<P>I have found MR2 turbo's on the street relatively slow, because they let their turbo's go over the recommended mileage without rebuild, and they run only like 4 psi of boost. I have raced them, killed them off the line of course, and waited for their turbo's to spool up so they will catch up.  Well they usually don't because their turbo's need rebuilding.<P>I.E. why the vast majority of MR2 turbo's on the market are WAY overpriced for what you get.  Your basically spending well over 8,000 for a car that will need atleast 1,000 in work just to make it perform like advertised.  2 pathetic.  I could get an 88 formula for 2,000, dump in a mildly built up 3.4 for 2,000, add a stage II Design One turbo for 4000, and even if your car is putting out 300 Hp at the crank, I am putting that out at the wheels for much cheaper.  Oh yeah, the insurance company will think you have some 135 Hp 2.8... <P>So the bottom line is, be a ricer, or be a racer...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
