Z||000071||1FST2M6||12-18-2000||10:53 AM||||ok  what year is said MR2? from 11-89 to 10-93 ALL MR2 turbos were spec with 220bhp running a CUTE Garret CT26 dual enrty intake(8.5-11psi). in 11-93 they went to 245bhp running 13psi out of a 3sgte @ 13psi. running a SMALLER turbo a Garett CT-20. what JAP Spec motor are you talking about? they are ALL the same 3SGT-E the only difference was in the the turbo and non turbo (5SFE) was the ceramic coating on the piston and the head. just like in the 4AGZ-E and the 4AG that was in the MR2 S/C and the AE-86 Corolla GT-S/Z ONLY Jap and aussie spec cars recieved these motors.. but are easy to get and CHEAP to install here. I heard an MR2 owner tell me he had a T-67 on his car.. uum HA,   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> i about pee-d my pants when i heard that.. at 6200rpm at 80% volumetric effiency that tiny motor is pumping enough air to turn that BIG GULP sized turbine.. at 7400rpm at 80% effiency it'll ramp up and become positive pressure. THEN start making power. uum not sure what he was smokin' but he needs to share with the rest of us... ok yeah HE may have had one on his car but he'd have to have an INSANE balance job done to keep it from self destructing at 10,000rpm  just to realize ANY usable power. <P>sorry just playing with the calculator and adding my $.02 <P>so what "Jap Spec" motor are you replacing your current 3sgte with? the 1UZF-E or the  7MGT-E? thoze are about the only thing worth throwing your $ at... oh if your' not sure what they are... the 1UZF-E is the 300hp V8 from the Lexus LS and the 7MGTE is from the Supra Turbo/Soarer(not he twin turbo.. the 86-93 the forged crank version of the new one) <P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000072||Oreif||12-18-2000||11:03 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CUTTER:<BR><B>uh...to get the motor rebuilt!? I need it faster. It has 116000 miles. I figure, rebuild now...it will last for as long as I have it! Or if i can find a jap-spec motor to throw in for under $2000 I will do that! has to be under 40,000 miles! japsec are 230 hp stock!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No flames here... But, If I were to guess You bought the MR2 for $5000, $140 for the ALT, $12 for the valve cover gasket, Turbo rebuild is what roughly $500, Motor Rebuild is around $3500 (parts and labor) So you are somewhere around $9000 invested.<BR>So lets compare, (Friends car built this summer)<BR>87 GT $2000, V-8 Archie kit $3500, $2800 for a slightly used (12K miles) V-8 at 330hp.<BR>UNDER $9000 and I'll bet faster than your car. More reliable. Sounds better than a wound-up turbo 4-cyl. (my opinion)<P>Thing is maybe if you'd have spent that kind of money on a Fiero you already had, you'd have had a killer car. I'm sure that any car that had a budget of $4000 could be boosted in performance to pass your MR2. <BR>I'm not flaming MR2's (driven both gen's) I personally don't like to drive them. It's my preference. I have seen a few posted here and ones on the MR2 board that look great and probably are pretty quick. I can respect anyone who has a car they are proud of and take's great care of it. (sounds like you enjoy beating on your cars on a regular basis)<BR>But to sell parts in a condition that is not as advertised, Then trash others car's is very immature. <BR>In the spring why don't you bring your car to Blackhawk Farms Race Course and we'll see how you car deals with a few curves. I already know my lap times and I know the lap times of many other cars, including MR2's, Porsche, Mazda, F-bodies, Vettes, and Mustangs.<P>By the way mine is a stock 2.8L with sprint manifolds and an automatic trans with a shiftkit.<BR>Not fast 0-60 but will out corner your car easily.<P>"Happines is not around the corner......<BR>Happiness IS the corner."<P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000073||GT Bastard||12-18-2000||06:43 PM||||Hey Cutter, I thought your smoke was due to a leaky valve cover gasket?  And why's it in the shop?  I thought you knew your stuff, big-shooter.||||reg||1
